  "notes": "Waiver filing, cash basis, Exhibit A all-funds statement (10/1/21-9/30/22), pp1-4; p5 schedules of investments, debt and interfund transfers. General, Street, Community Events, Community Center, Keno and Payroll Clearing funds governmental (as in FY2023/FY2024; no Debt Service fund column this year); Water and Sewer business-type, including the Debt Service row (line 39) printed only in the Water and Sewer columns. Governmental beginning/ending cash = line 3 / line 24 subtotals (net cash + investments); investments shown separately for information. County treasurer balances printed below the statement (628.99 at 10/1/21, 769.20 at 9/30/22) are not part of the line 24/28 balances and are not added (as in FY2023). Other Capital Outlay prints no function: labelled Capital Outlay. Community Development kept as economic development (as in FY2023/FY2024). Local Receipts: Other is a context label and stays other (Keno column 425,843.95 included). Transfers per p5: General -> Water 78,000, Sewer 17,000, Streets 12,000, Community Center 14,000; Community Events -> General 3,509.22; Keno -> General 220,000. Governmental roll: 2,336,860.52 + 571,320.64 - 363,404.24 + 249,509.22 - 344,509.22 = 2,449,776.92. Business: 44,809.14 + 139,234.45 - 235,279.21 + 95,000 = 43,764.38. Outstanding debt (p5): refunding bond 320,000, NDEQ note 137,916 (schedule only). Read pages 1-5 of 5"
